    title: "Half the puzzles are impossible", scenario: "Boards are generated by shuffling all sixteen tiles uniformly at random. Roughly 50% of users cannot finish, ending with exactly two tiles transposed. What is wrong and what is the fix?",
    options: ["Reachable states are half the space (a parity invariant of inversions plus the blank's row is preserved by every move) — generate by walking random LEGAL moves from the solved state, or swap two non-blank tiles to repair parity", "The shuffle is biased and needs a better random number generator", "The solver's heuristic rejects valid boards and should be relaxed", "Some tiles were rendered in the wrong orientation"],
