    options: ["Admissibility — a heuristic that can exceed the true remaining cost breaks the optimality proof, so A* may return a longer-than-shortest solution (bounded by the weight, hence 'weighted A*')", "Nothing: any monotonically increasing transform of an admissible heuristic stays admissible", "Termination — the search may now loop forever on solvable boards", "Memory — the open list grows because f values are larger"],
